Snipload is free to use. It is not open source. The source code is public so that anyone can
check what the program does - not so that it can be copied, re-released or reused.

"Snipload" below means the program, its source code, its interface and design, its texts and
translations, its name and its logo.


1. What you may do

   a) Download Snipload from the official page, https://github.com/Mavi-05/Snipload, and use
      it free of charge, privately and for your work. The clips you make with it are not
      covered by this license; what you may do with them depends on the rights to the videos
      you clip.
   b) Read the source code.
   c) Recommend Snipload and link to the official page, as long as it stays clear that it is
      Snipload by Mavi-05.


2. What you may not do without written permission from the author

   a) Copy Snipload or parts of it into another program, project, website or product.
   b) Pass Snipload on or offer it for download anywhere other than the official page. This
      includes re-uploads, mirrors, installers, download portals and bundles with other
      software.
   c) Change Snipload and publish or pass on the changed version. This includes renamed,
      re-skinned, translated and repackaged versions.
   d) Present, advertise or promote Snipload, a copy of it or a changed version of it as your
      own work, under your own name or under a different name.
   e) Sell, rent or license Snipload, charge for access to it, or earn money in any other way
      by offering the program itself.
   f) Use the name "Snipload" or the logo for another program, website, channel or product,
      or in a way that suggests it comes from the author or is approved by the author.
   g) Remove or change this license, the name of the author or any copyright notice.


3. GitHub

   The repository is hosted on GitHub. As GitHub's Terms of Service require for public
   repositories, you may view it and fork it on GitHub. That is the only copy this license
   allows beyond section 1, and a fork gives you no right to do anything listed in section 2.


4. Software from others

   Snipload contains and downloads software, fonts and icons made by others (among them
   yt-dlp, ffmpeg, whisper.cpp, Real-ESRGAN, hls.js, Lucide and several fonts). They stay
   under their own licenses, which are listed in src/snipload/web/LICENSES.txt and in the app
   under Settings > Licenses. Nothing in this license limits the rights those licenses give
   you for those parts.


5. End of permission

   If you do anything listed in section 2, your permission under section 1 ends immediately.
   The author may have copies taken down and may take the steps the law provides.


6. No warranty

   SNIPLOAD IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING
